Hi @bailejl and everyone experiencing this issue! 

Thank you for reporting this. You're absolutely right - Claude Code 1.0.51+ has introduced breaking changes to the settings.json format, particularly around hooks. Here's what's happening and how to fix it:

## The Problem

Claude Code 1.0.51 changed the hooks format from the object-based structure that Claude Flow was generating:
```json
// Old format (what Claude Flow generates)
"hooks": {
  "preEditHook": { "command": "npx", "args": [...] },
  "postEditHook": { "command": "npx", "args": [...] }
}
```

To the new array-based format:
```json
// New format (what Claude Code 1.0.51+ expects)
"hooks": {
  "PreToolUse": [
    {
      "matcher": "Edit|Write",
      "hooks": [{"type": "command", "command": "npx claude-flow hooks pre-edit"}]
    }
  ],
  "PostToolUse": [...]
}
```

