## 🚀 Additional Requirements: Parallel Workflow Execution & Complex Agent Architectures

### Parallel Non-Interactive Workflows

The automation system should support running multiple parallel workflows concurrently using non-interactive capabilities, **without modifying** the existing swarm or hive-mind functionality. This enables implementation of complex agent architectures like MLE-Star and other novel workflows.

### Key Design Principles

1. **Preserve Existing Systems**: Swarm and hive-mind commands remain unchanged
2. **Parallel Execution**: Multiple workflows can run concurrently in separate processes
3. **Complex Architectures**: Support for advanced patterns like MLE-Star, Tree-of-Thoughts, etc.
4. **Non-Interactive by Default**: All automation workflows run without user intervention

### Implementation Architecture

```typescript
// New workflow executor that runs independently of swarm/hive-mind
class ParallelWorkflowExecutor {
  private activeWorkflows: Map<string, WorkflowInstance> = new Map();

  async executeParallel(workflows: WorkflowDefinition[], options: ExecutionOptions) {
    // Each workflow runs in its own process/thread
    const promises = workflows.map(workflow => 
      this.executeWorkflow(workflow, {
        ...options,
        nonInteractive: true,
        claude: true,
        isolated: true  // Don't interfere with swarm/hive-mind
      })
    );

    // Execute all workflows concurrently
    return Promise.all(promises);
  }

  private async executeWorkflow(workflow: WorkflowDefinition, options: ExecutionOptions) {
    // Spawn isolated Claude instance for this workflow
    const claudeProcess = spawn('claude', [
      '--non-interactive',
      '--prompt', this.generateWorkflowPrompt(workflow)
    ], {
      detached: true,  // Run independently
      stdio: ['pipe', 'pipe', 'pipe']
    });

    // Track without interfering with global state
    this.activeWorkflows.set(workflow.id, {
      process: claudeProcess,
      workflow,
      startTime: Date.now()
    });
  }
}
```

