Here is one possible fix to the better-sqlite3 database connection error has been successfully resolved. Here's what was implemented:

  Root Cause

  The error occurred in .../node_modules/claude-flow/src/cli/simple-commands/hive-mind/session-manager.js at line 932 in
  the removeChildPid method. The method was trying to call this.db.prepare() without checking if the database connection was still open, causing a "database
  connection is not open" error during session cleanup.

  Solution Applied

  Added proper database connection validation and error handling to three critical methods:

  1. removeChildPid() - Added connection check and try/catch error handling
  2. addChildPid() - Added the same protection pattern
  3. getChildPids() - Added connection validation for read operations

  Error Handling Pattern

  // Check if database connection is still open
  if (!this.db) {
    console.warn('Database connection not available for [operation] operation');
    return false;
  }

  try {
    // Database operations...
  } catch (error) {
    if (error.message.includes('database connection is not open') || error.message.includes('database is closed')) {
      console.warn(`Database connection closed during [operation] operation: ${error.message}`);
      return false;
    }
    // Re-throw other errors
    throw error;
  }

  Testing Results

  - ✅ hive-mind init - Database initialization works
  - ✅ hive-mind spawn - Session creation and management works
  - ✅ hive-mind stop - Session cleanup and PID removal works without errors
  - ✅ No more "database connection is not open" errors during shutdown

  The fix ensures graceful handling of database operations during session lifecycle management, preventing crashes when the database connection is closed during
  cleanup operations (like when pressing Ctrl+C to stop a session).

