## Fix

Defect **GV-001** in [claude-flow-patch](https://github.com/sparkling/claude-flow-patch).

**Root cause:** `memory delete` removes the key-value entry from the store but does not call `hnswIndex.markDelete()`, leaving orphan vectors that appear in subsequent similarity searches.

1 find/replace in `memory/memory-initializer.ts`. After the SQLite soft-delete in `deleteEntry()`, remove the entry from the persisted HNSW metadata file and the in-memory map.

> File paths reference TypeScript source (`.ts`) in the repo at `v3/@claude-flow/cli/src/`. Code blocks show compiled `.js` output — apply equivalent changes to the `.ts` source.

### Root Cause

`deleteEntry()` soft-deletes the SQLite row (`SET status = 'deleted'`) but never touches the HNSW index. The search code (`searchHNSWIndex`) iterates HNSW results and looks up metadata from `hnswIndex.entries` Map — ghost vectors still have metadata, so they appear in results.

Each CLI invocation is a fresh Node.js process, so the module-level `hnswIndex` variable is `null`. The fix must operate on the persisted metadata file (`hnsw.metadata.json`) directly, not just the in-memory Map.

### `memory/memory-initializer.ts` — Remove HNSW entry on delete

**Find:**
~~~javascript
        // Get remaining count
        const countResult = db.exec(`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM memory_entries WHERE status = 'active'`);
        const remainingEntries = countResult[0]?.values?.[0]?.[0] || 0;
        // Save updated database
~~~

**Replace with:**
~~~javascript
        // Remove ghost vector from HNSW metadata file
        const entryId = String(checkResult[0].values[0][0]);
        try {
            const swarmDir = path.join(process.cwd(), '.swarm');
            const metadataPath = path.join(swarmDir, 'hnsw.metadata.json');
            if (fs.existsSync(metadataPath)) {
                const metadata = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(metadataPath, 'utf-8'));
                const filtered = metadata.filter(([id]) => id !== entryId);
                if (filtered.length < metadata.length) {
                    fs.writeFileSync(metadataPath, JSON.stringify(filtered));
                }
            }
        } catch { /* best-effort */ }
        // Also clear in-memory index if loaded
        if (hnswIndex?.entries?.has(entryId)) {
            hnswIndex.entries.delete(entryId);
        }
        // Get remaining count
        const countResult = db.exec(`SELECT COUNT(*) FROM memory_entries WHERE status = 'active'`);
        const remainingEntries = countResult[0]?.values?.[0]?.[0] || 0;
        // Save updated database
~~~

### Note

The `@ruvector/core` HNSW index doesn't support point removal, so the vector remains in the index. However, `searchHNSWIndex` already skips entries missing from the metadata Map (`if (!entry) continue`), so removing from the metadata is sufficient to suppress ghost results.

